# .vscodeignore — what `vsce package` leaves OUT of the .vsix.
# The .vsix ships five root files — package.json, README.md, CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE and, since M6
# item 23c, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md (the codicons' attribution) — and dist/: the host bundle
# dist/extension.js and, under dist/webview/, one bundle per view beside the codicon stylesheet and
# font (plan §11.3; `npx vsce ls --no-dependencies` lists them, and test/unit/vsix.test.ts pins the
# root list on every `npm test`). Sources, tests, tooling, both worlds' source maps and node_modules
# stay behind. Root tooling files are named one by one below, so a new root file SHIPS unless a line
# here leaves it out — run `vsce ls` after adding one.
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.vscode-test.mjs
.github/**
src/**
test/**
docs/**
scripts/**
out/**
coverage/**
node_modules/**
# The source maps of both worlds: a user's VS Code never reads them; the dev host reads them from
# this folder's dist/, not from a .vsix.
**/*.map
# `npm run analyze` leaves its raw metafile (both bundles' records) next to the bundles; it is a
# report, not code.
dist/meta.json
**/*.ts
esbuild.mjs
eslint.config.mjs
vitest.config.mts
tsconfig*.json
.gitignore
pr-cascade-plan.md
**/*.vsix
# Claude Code skill definitions (.claude/skills/**): tooling for the agent, not for users.
.claude/**
